<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The watch app's own strings, in the source language.

  English is the source here for the same reason it is on the phone: it is the language
  the code is written in, and every other language is a translation of it. A translator
  adds res/values-<code>/strings.xml and fills in the same identifiers; nothing else
  needs to change. See wearos/README.md.

  Two rules that matter more here than on a phone. Keep it short – this is a round
  480 pixel face read at arm's length, and a label that wraps to three lines is a label
  that is not read. And leave the aviation vocabulary alone: NOTAM, METAR, FIS, QNH and
  the frequencies are the same words in every cockpit, and a pilot looking for "NOTAM"
  is not helped by a translation of it.
-->
